## 4. HARN / HARN2 / PV1 — if fixtures review

  Review only. Disk is the source. Do not edit those files.

  HARN reads:

    ooda/fixtures/wasm_if_true.oo
    ooda/scripts/wasm_if_true_smoke.oo

  Body must be only `if true { println("then-yes"); } else { println("else-no"); }`.
  Smoke must drive `./oodac/oodac`.
  After parent rebuild: wasmtime (if present) prints `then-yes` and not `else-no`.
  If wasmtime is missing, the bytes name `fd_write` and `then-yes`.
  Dummy `02 00 0b` fails this lock.

  HARN2 reads:

    ooda/fixtures/wasm_if_false.oo
    ooda/scripts/wasm_if_false_smoke.oo

  Body must be only `if false { println("then-no"); } else { println("else-yes"); }`.
  Smoke must drive `./oodac/oodac`.
  After parent rebuild: wasmtime prints `else-yes` and not `then-no`.
  Dummy `02 00 0b` fails this lock.

  PV1 reads:

    ooda/fixtures/wasm_if_hostile.oo
    ooda/scripts/wasm_if_hostile_smoke.oo

  Body is `let x = true; if x { println("fold-me"); } else { println("other"); }`.
  Condition is IDENT. It is not KW_TRUE.
  Dummy `end` or empty wasmtime stdout is honest.
  A fold-me-only body fails this lock.

## 5. INT — existing locks

  INT does not own the three if smokes. Those stay with HARN, HARN2, and PV1.

  After the parent rebuild, INT re-runs these locks on `./oodac/oodac`:

    scripts/wasm_hello_smoke.oo
    scripts/wasm_hello_hostile_smoke.oo
    scripts/wasm_print_lit_smoke.oo
    scripts/wasm_ident_lit_smoke.oo
    scripts/wasm_strcat_n_smoke.oo
    scripts/wasm_strcat_hostile_smoke.oo
    scripts/wasm_strcat_mixed_smoke.oo
    scripts/wasm_two_println_smoke.oo
    scripts/wasm_two_println_hostile_smoke.oo
    scripts/wasm_int_lit_smoke.oo

  Keep green. Do not weaken to magic-only.

  Support (keep green):

    scripts/open_wasm_binary_smoke.oo
    scripts/wasm_wat_honest_smoke.oo
    scripts/bit_identical_emit_lock.oo

  `fixtures/wasm_strcat_n.oo` is absent. N-join lock is `wasm_strcat3_lit.oo`.
  Mixed ident concat stays dummy. Hostile second print stays dummy.

## 6. SEC / MEM / RT — ovf, buf, dummy

  SEC reads overflow fail-closed. Own `openOODA/audit/wasm_sec.oot`.
  Lock: `scripts/wasm_fail_closed_smoke.oo`.
  emit_n must not assign `oo_wasm_ovf = 0` at entry.
  Check still runs before emit-wasm.

  MEM reads oversized print. Own `openOODA/audit/wasm_mem.oot`.
  Lock: `scripts/wasm_buf_smoke.oo`.
  A 30000-byte print is `ERR wasm buf`. No dummy `\0asm`.

  RT reads dummy end and the emit_n ovf path. Own `openOODA/audit/wasm_rt.oot`.
  Non-print functions keep body `02 00 0b`.
  If ovf is set, emit_n writes `ERR wasm buf` and no canned module.

  These three roles do not edit runtime this wave.

## 7. DE1 / DE2 — fold, two, int unchanged

  DE1 re-reads `ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_fold.oo`.
  `wasm_fold_hello` stays the exact hello main match.
  Extra statements miss. No-let misses. Do not edit that file.

  DE2 re-reads `ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_two.oo` and `ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_int.oo`.
  Two-println stays two STRING prints then RBRACE.
  Int-lit stays one `println(INT)` then RBRACE.
  Do not edit those files. Do not add runtime if.

## 8. HYG — line counts

  Count `ooda/oodac/wasm_emit*.oo`, `ooda/scripts/wasm_*_smoke.oo`,
  and `ooda/fixtures/wasm_*.oo`.
  Cap is 256. Comments count.
  Write only `openOODA/audit/wasm_hyg.oot`.
  Split only if a counted file is over 256 and this wave names that file.
  `wasm_emit_if.oo` is 121. No split.

## 9. DOCS / PV2 — boards

  DOCS writes leftover WASM sentences on SHIPPED.oot and ROADMAP.oot
  only after the parent rebuild and after INT plus if-review notes exist.
  Also writes `openOODA/audit/wasm_docs.oot`.
  Keep dummy `end` residual. Keep the browser host residual.
  Keep C emit + gcc everyday. Do not sell a complete WASM backend.

  PV2 writes only `openOODA/audit/wasm_pv2.oot`.
  PV2 does not edit SHIPPED.oot or ROADMAP.oot.
  Check that those boards still name dummy `end` residual,
  a residual browser host, C emit + gcc everyday,
  and not a complete WASM backend.

